  "purpose": "M2's scenario (planning/mvp-m2-plan.md, Scenarios and the harness, Q12): Instance 3 of security model v1 on M0's two Linux domains, each on its own hart: G0, the untrusted host (host_t), and G1, the protected domain (prot_t); a request page the host writes and the protected domain reads, a response page the protected domain writes and the host reads, and a secret page that only the protected domain's root maps; the one management grant, which lets the host pause or terminate the protected domain; the secret; the measured domain; the denied accesses; the management calls with their results; the requests; and the expected outcomes of the scenario and its four runtime negative images. Its two build-time negative images are in negatives/.",
  "trust": "Data only. tools/policy-check.py runs A1 to A6 and A8, with A7 vacuous, on policy.te with this labeling, these need sets, and this manifest (domains, monitor objects, pages, management grants, the secret, and the measurement's inputs), and writes the authority report; tools/gen-scenario.py writes no header unless that check passes, then checks the rest against src/mvp-layout.h and tools/gen-dts.py, computes the expected measurement over the build outputs, and emits the build header and the checkers' expectation files from it; a change is a rebuild, never a run-time selection. The secret is a public test value (Q5): the denied accesses and the results that depend on it show confidentiality, not its secrecy.",
  "scope": "M2. Types, labels, domain indices, hart IDs, VMIDs, and GPAs are identifiers, not authority (S1 H03): only the sealed record, the leaves a hart installs, and the sealed management grants that hart 0 alone consults grant anything.",
